# About page

Add an About page only when background, responsibility or scope would overload the project page. It states what the work covers, what it leaves out and how its status is kept current. For example, a fictional documentation project can say it covers the lighting guides and excludes alarm settings. A small project needs only a short About section on the same page. The parent is [Topical events](../topical-events.html).

## When to use it

Use it only when background, responsibility or scope would overload the main project page. Say what the work covers, what it excludes and how its status is maintained.

## Structure and behaviour

Link back to the parent project and keep stable background apart from dated progress notes. Name the document owner by role rather than publishing personal information. Use real dates for public documentation and label specimen dates as examples.

## Home Assistant boundary

This is not a claim of government authority or a live project-management system. Do not duplicate status text in two places unless both share one source. Keep operational controls on their native pages.

